.\" Everything in mc.1 below the generated command list. Raw roff, emitted
.\" verbatim by `xtask man` — escape literal hyphens as \- yourself.
.SH PLUGIN COMMANDS
The commands above are core's. Plugins contribute their own, which is why
.B mc help
and this page can disagree with what
.B mc
will actually accept:
.B mc plugins
is the authority on an installed system.
.PP
The packages this repository ships add:
.TP
.B mc rcon
An RCON console, or one command against a running server. Also makes a stop
warn players first and a backup consistent \(em see
.BR mc-rcon (1).
.TP
.B mc backup\fR, \fBmc restore
Timestamped archives and restores, on a timer or on demand \(em see
.BR mc-backup (1).
.TP
.B mc install \fIpack\fB.mrpack
Install or upgrade from a Modrinth modpack \(em see
.BR mc-mrpack (1).
.SH SYSTEMD INTEGRATION
.B minecraft.service
runs the server.
.B mc start\fR, \fBstop\fR, \fBrestart\fR, \fBstatus
and
.B logs
drive it through
.BR systemctl (1)
and
.BR journalctl (1),
and exist because they add what those cannot: an EULA gate, a graceful
countdown, and a start that waits for the JVM to settle rather than reporting
success the moment the process forks.
.PP
Three subcommands are the unit's own and are not for interactive use:
.TP
.B mc serve
.BR ExecStart= .
Runs the server in the foreground. This is also what a container entrypoint
wants, on a host with no systemd at all.
.TP
.B mc shutdown
.BR ExecStop= .
Warns players, stops gracefully, waits for the world to flush.
.TP
.B mc reload
.BR ExecReload= .
Asks the running server to reload its configuration.
.PP
All three run as the
.B minecraft
user under
.BR ProtectSystem=strict ,
not as root, and write nothing outside
.IR /opt/minecraft .
.PP
.BR "systemctl start minecraft" (1)
bypasses mc entirely, which is why the EULA and
.I server.properties
gates live in
.B mc serve
rather than in
.BR "mc start" .
Starting the unit by hand is safe; it fails the same way.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 78
.RB ( EX_CONFIG ,
see
.BR sysexits (3))
Something an operator must fix: an unaccepted EULA, an unreadable
.IR server.properties ,
a missing
.IR server.jar ,
a malformed config file, or input that failed validation \(em a hostile modpack
or a backup archive containing a symlink.
.IP
The unit maps this to
.BR RestartPreventExitStatus= ,
so
.B mc serve
fails visibly without restart-looping over something no restart can fix.
.TP
.B 1
Anything else, including a refused privilege check and a lock held by another
mc operation. From
.BR "mc serve" ,
a genuine crash \(em the unit restarts after
.BR RestartSec= .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MC_ROOT
Prefix for every path below. Exists for the test suite and for images that
stage a tree somewhere other than
.IR / .
Production is unset, which means
.IR / .
.TP
.B SUDO_USER
Read only to decide whether a re-exec under
.BR sudo (8)
has already happened.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/minecraft/config.toml
mc's configuration. A dpkg conffile: your edits survive upgrades. See
.BR mc-config (5).
.TP
.I /etc/minecraft/server.passwd
The RCON password,
.BR "root:minecraft 0640" .
Never passed in argv, where
.I /proc/<pid>/cmdline
would expose it to every local user.
.TP
.I /opt/minecraft/
The server and its world,
.BR "minecraft:minecraft 0750" .
The only
.B ReadWritePaths=
the unit grants.
.TP
.I /opt/minecraft/server.properties
The game's configuration,
.BR "minecraft:minecraft 0640" .
Owner matters as much as mode: root-owned, the JVM can neither read nor write
it, comes up on compiled-in defaults, and generates a stray world beside the
real one.
.TP
.I /var/backups/minecraft/
Backup archives,
.BR "root:root 0700" .
Deliberately not the service account: that account runs untrusted mods.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/mc/plugins.d/
Plugin manifests. See
.BR mc-plugins (5).
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/mc/
Plugin executables. Not on
.BR PATH :
they are invoked by mc, and are not a command surface.
.TP
.I /run/minecraft/mc.lock
Serialises install, upgrade, backup and restore against each other.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install a Paper server, unattended \(em both consents given, so nothing
prompts:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo mc install \-\-type paper \-\-accept\-eula \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
Upgrade to the newest version of the configured type, taking a backup first:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo mc upgrade
.fi
.RE
.PP
Follow the log, then stop with a five-minute in-game countdown:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mc logs
sudo mc stop
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read the manual for a command a plugin contributed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mc man backup
.fi
.RE
